# Real bug fixed here (2026-09-13): core.autocrlf=true on a Windows dev
# machine converts app/mvnw's shebang line ("#!/bin/sh") to CRLF on every
# local checkout/clone, corrupting it to "#!/bin/sh\r\n" -- which then
# fails "no such file or directory" the moment anything tries to execute
# it on Linux (the shell interprets the interpreter path as literally
# "/bin/sh\r", which does not exist). This broke agent/demo_execution.py's
# create_isolated_workspace() (a fresh git clone, done on this machine)
# feeding a real Railway build for the first time this project ever
# deployed a Java change through that pipeline (see docs/LESSONS.md and
# docs/ACTION_QUEUE.json's ACT-008 entry). Forcing LF here, regardless of
# any given machine's core.autocrlf setting, is the standard, durable fix
# -- not something every future clone/developer needs to remember.
app/mvnw       text eol=lf
app/.mvn/**    text eol=lf
